@startuml recent-loss-episode-state
title Signal-Loss Episode — Redis Key State (CP1)

skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

[*] --> NO_EPISODE

NO_EPISODE --> ACTIVE : Alert Evaluator scan detects\nsilence >= SIGNAL_LOSS_THRESHOLD_MS\n(alert-state:{entity_id} written)

ACTIVE --> RECENT : entity resumes\n(Position Consumer MULTI:\nHSET recent-loss + PEXPIRE + DEL alert-state)

RECENT --> NO_EPISODE : COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS\nelapses — Redis TTL expiry\n(retention bound, not eligibility)

RECENT --> NO_EPISODE : entity goes dark again before\nrecent-loss expires — a NEW ACTIVE\nepisode opens independently

note right of ACTIVE
  alert-state:{entity_id}
  No TTL. Anchored by dark_since_ms.
  composite_issued = '0' reserved for
  Phase 06 composite correlation.
end note

note right of RECENT
  recent-loss:{entity_id}
  TTL = COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS,
  counted from resumed_at_ms.
  This is retention only — actual composite
  eligibility is a separate source-time check
  (see correlation-window-semantics).
end note

note bottom of NO_EPISODE
  No Redis key exists for this entity's
  signal-loss state. A future silence opens
  a brand new ACTIVE episode with a new
  dark_since_ms and a new deterministic alert_id.
end note

@enduml
